From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mortyzhaoyu <morty.zhaoyu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 15:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mpp: rkvdec2: don't oops when the IOMMU is missing

If the rkvdec IOMMU fails to probe, mpp_dev_probe() sets iommu_info to
NULL and continues. rkvdec2_alloc_rcbbuf() then dereferences
iommu_info->domain (NULL + 0x40) and the deferred-probe worker oopses;
a second oops follows in rkvdec_vdpu383_reset() from runtime suspend
because link_dec was never initialised. Bail out cleanly in both paths.

---
--- a/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_rkvdec2.c
+++ b/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_rkvdec2.c
@@ -1418,6 +1418,10 @@
 	int ret = 0;
 	u32 irq_status = 0;
 
+	/* link table mode not initialised (e.g. probe failed early) */
+	if (!link)
+		return 0;
+
 	mpp_debug_enter();
 
 	/* disable irq */
@@ -1697,6 +1701,12 @@
 	struct iommu_domain *domain;
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
 
+	/* RCB needs a working IOMMU; bail out cleanly instead of oopsing */
+	if (!dec->mpp.iommu_info) {
+		dev_warn(dev, "no iommu attached, skip rcb buffer\n");
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
+
 	/* get rcb iova start and size */
 	ret = device_property_read_u32_array(dev, "rockchip,rcb-iova", vals, 2);
 	if (ret) {

-- 
